@gmaynez FWIW: I tried your 'opencode models --refresh', but its provided definition didn't allow for switching the glm-5.2 thinking level variants that z.ai had posted in their coding plan announcement for 5.2; I had already created my own opencode.json definition which added their two definitions (& allowed for switching between 'variants'/thinking levels in opencode/tui), though I didn't bother specifying the other fields yet:

[inserted just above 'options' w/o specifying 'reasoningEffort' in that section]
... 
                                "variants": {
                                        "high": {
                                                "reasoningEffort": "high"
                                        },
                                        "max": {
                                                "reasoningEffort": "max"
                                        }
                                },
...

@rekram1-node @simonklee @malventano @marcusquinn quick follow-up: I checked the recent releases through OpenCode 1.17.6, and I do not see a related fix in 1.17.4 / 1.17.5 / 1.17.6.

This is still a deterministic Copilot `gpt-5.5` failure case for existing sessions after the active Copilot credential / Responses API connection changes: OpenCode keeps referencing stale stored `metadata.openai.itemId` values and Copilot rejects them with `input item ID does not belong to this connection`.

Could someone please take a look at invalidating or not reusing stored Responses API item IDs when the active Copilot credential changes?
